1
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:47,900
[KING OF COMEDY]

2
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:50,900
[Episode 23]

3
00:01:58,070 --> 00:01:58,710
Mr. Huang!

4
00:02:00,040 --> 00:02:01,280
You scared me.

5
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:04,280
There's something else
that might scare you even more.

6
00:02:04,280 --> 00:02:04,880
What is it?

7
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:06,760
All the people

8
00:02:07,280 --> 00:02:08,190
in Shapu Village

9
00:02:08,190 --> 00:02:09,150
have signed.

10
00:02:09,310 --> 00:02:10,360
All of them?

11
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:12,270
Let me see! Let me see!

12
00:02:13,310 --> 00:02:14,240
It's true.

13
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,430
What about Zhen? Did she sign?

14
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:17,980
Zhen... Here.

15
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:20,190
Right, right, over there.

16
00:02:20,190 --> 00:02:21,400
-But Mr. Huang…
-Great.

17
00:02:21,400 --> 00:02:22,470
Let me tell you.

18
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:25,260
Only one person didn't sign.

19
00:02:25,260 --> 00:02:27,450
It's that fool
who threw shells the other day.

20
00:02:27,450 --> 00:02:28,840
You're demolishing the village

21
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,840
just for the treasure underground.

22
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:32,360
It doesn't matter. It doesn't matter.

23
00:02:32,360 --> 00:02:33,620
He's the only one left.

24
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,560
Do you know

25
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:35,840
how much time this little Shapu Village

26
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:37,470
has wasted?

27
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:38,840
This time, I'm telling you,

28
00:02:38,840 --> 00:02:39,800
it's done!

29
00:02:39,829 --> 00:02:40,900
Mr. Huang, it has to be done.

30
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:42,410
You never fail at anything.

31
00:02:42,410 --> 00:02:43,410
So here,

32
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:44,430
I

33
00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:46,190
congratulate my dear Mr. Huang

34
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:47,590
on acquiring Shapu Village.

35
00:02:47,590 --> 00:02:48,590
Let's celebrate.

36
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:51,850
Does it hurt?

37
00:02:57,590 --> 00:02:58,800
-It's fine.
-Let me tell you.

38
00:02:58,800 --> 00:02:59,800
Once this pier is built,

39
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:01,150
in the future, you know,

40
00:03:01,510 --> 00:03:03,950
I mean, just, you know,

41
00:03:03,970 --> 00:03:05,000
just, just...

42
00:03:05,160 --> 00:03:05,890
Look at this.

43
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:07,680
When this pier is built in the future,

44
00:03:07,680 --> 00:03:09,080
this first shop will be yours.

45
00:03:09,080 --> 00:03:11,080
You can just count your money there.

46
00:03:12,190 --> 00:03:13,520
Where is the first shop?

47
00:03:13,680 --> 00:03:15,050
Right here. Look closely.

48
00:03:15,050 --> 00:03:16,000
The first one at the entrance.

49
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:16,930
The whole shop

50
00:03:16,950 --> 00:03:17,910
is yours.

51
00:03:18,190 --> 00:03:20,150
Thank you, my dearest Mr. Huang.

52
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,750
I'm so grateful to you.

53
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:24,960
But I have to criticize you.

54
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:26,490
Look at your physical condition.

55
00:03:26,490 --> 00:03:27,190
It's not only about you.

56
00:03:27,190 --> 00:03:27,840
It belongs to all of us.

57
00:03:27,840 --> 00:03:30,370
You can't keep
eating these instant noodles.

58
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:31,880
Braised pork flavor?

59
00:03:32,240 --> 00:03:33,329
And you added chili?

60
00:03:33,329 --> 00:03:33,920
What else?

61
00:03:33,920 --> 00:03:35,650
Why not get spicy beef noodles?

62
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:38,760
I eat instant noodles

63
00:03:38,870 --> 00:03:40,240
to save some money.

64
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:41,930
I'll take all this money

65
00:03:42,070 --> 00:03:44,120
and throw it
right in front of that Ma woman.

66
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,400
I want to tell her...

67
00:03:46,800 --> 00:03:48,030
that I am capable.

68
00:03:48,560 --> 00:03:49,360
You are very capable.

69
00:03:49,360 --> 00:03:51,190
It's time to show your capability.

70
00:03:51,190 --> 00:03:51,800
Hurry up

71
00:03:51,800 --> 00:03:52,910
and go through the procedures

72
00:03:52,910 --> 00:03:54,310
to avoid any long delays.

73
00:03:55,910 --> 00:03:56,750
The shop

74
00:03:56,870 --> 00:03:57,630
is yours.

75
00:03:58,070 --> 00:03:58,710
When the time comes,

76
00:03:58,710 --> 00:04:00,430
I'll prepare all these instant noodles
for you.

77
00:04:00,430 --> 00:04:01,400
I'll head over.

78
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:04,000
Careful.

79
00:04:04,280 --> 00:04:05,880
Why do you have so much stuff?

80
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:09,590
Chaoyue,

81
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:11,280
do you think we can

82
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:13,860
go back to the village
to visit in the future?

83
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,680
We'll never be able
to come back in this lifetime.

84
00:04:16,680 --> 00:04:18,310
The last truck! Thank you!

85
00:04:19,120 --> 00:04:20,720
You're welcome. It's my job.

86
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:22,560
Ms. Manyu.

87
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:24,000
Are you moving today?

88
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,130
Yes. What about you?

89
00:04:25,190 --> 00:04:26,390
I'm moving tomorrow.

90
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:28,310
Come, let me help you.

91
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:30,000
Careful, careful.

92
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:31,270
Okay, thanks.

93
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:45,490
Everyone has moved.

94
00:04:46,070 --> 00:04:47,480
We have to move too.

95
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:49,500
[Shapu Village Station]

96
00:05:04,550 --> 00:05:06,870
What will I do when you leave, Yanzi?

97
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:10,010
How can I live without you?

98
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:11,070
Don't be frugal.

99
00:05:11,270 --> 00:05:12,870
Spend what you need to spend.

100
00:05:25,390 --> 00:05:27,790
Take care of yourself
in the future, Yanzi!

101
00:05:36,630 --> 00:05:37,120
Dad,

102
00:05:37,360 --> 00:05:38,950
you don't want this basket anymore?

103
00:05:38,950 --> 00:05:39,680
No.

104
00:05:40,070 --> 00:05:42,100
Then, what about the fridge?

105
00:05:42,830 --> 00:05:43,390
No.

106
00:05:43,390 --> 00:05:45,720
What about the orchids
you've grown for so many years?

107
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:46,390
No.

108
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:51,040
Dad, you don't want me either?

109
00:05:51,060 --> 00:05:53,790
It's Shapu Village
that doesn't want us anymore!

110
00:06:59,510 --> 00:07:01,240
Who dares to tear down my house?

111
00:07:12,170 --> 00:07:12,680
Sister.

112
00:07:14,490 --> 00:07:15,930
Maybe I should do it.

113
00:08:56,960 --> 00:08:58,560
Didn't expect this, did you?

114
00:08:59,150 --> 00:09:00,320
The first person

115
00:09:01,910 --> 00:09:03,080
who resisted you

116
00:09:04,590 --> 00:09:06,920
has now become
the first to respond to you.

117
00:09:08,550 --> 00:09:09,010
This...

118
00:09:09,630 --> 00:09:10,320
Let's go.

119
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:12,750
Go back and report to Mr. Huang.

120
00:09:14,380 --> 00:09:16,580
Deputy General Manager Chen, this way.

121
00:09:34,790 --> 00:09:35,990
Stop packing them up.

122
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:39,750
Come, come.

123
00:09:40,750 --> 00:09:41,270
Careful, careful.

124
00:09:41,270 --> 00:09:42,330
Careful, careful.

125
00:09:44,340 --> 00:09:45,460
They're all here.

126
00:09:45,510 --> 00:09:46,000
Okay.

127
00:09:46,150 --> 00:09:47,080
Tonight,

128
00:09:47,320 --> 00:09:49,300
no one leaves until we finish eating.

129
00:09:49,300 --> 00:09:50,010
Junnan.

130
00:09:50,870 --> 00:09:52,870
These are not expired.

131
00:09:53,600 --> 00:09:54,240
Right.

132
00:09:55,030 --> 00:09:56,080
Not used to it?

133
00:09:57,120 --> 00:09:57,910
I'll take them away.

134
00:09:57,910 --> 00:09:58,390
Don't!

135
00:09:58,390 --> 00:09:59,790
That's not what I meant.

136
00:09:59,960 --> 00:10:01,620
We can eat unexpired food too.

137
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:05,280
You're so sweet.

138
00:10:07,270 --> 00:10:08,030
Junnan.

139
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:10,130
After we distribute these,

140
00:10:10,150 --> 00:10:11,610
we're really breaking up?

141
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,200
What breaking up?

142
00:10:13,540 --> 00:10:15,070
Who said we're breaking up?

143
00:10:15,870 --> 00:10:17,320
We're just changing places.

144
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,200
When we go to the city,

145
00:10:18,200 --> 00:10:19,750
I'll still buy a villa.

146
00:10:21,150 --> 00:10:22,510
Buy a two-story one.

147
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:24,250
Three stories!

148
00:10:24,790 --> 00:10:26,030
Four or five stories!

149
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:27,480
It must be by the sea.

150
00:10:27,590 --> 00:10:28,320
Otherwise, I won't be used to it.

151
00:10:28,320 --> 00:10:29,630
Right, okay.

152
00:10:29,630 --> 00:10:33,000
Do you think
a 5-story villa is a bit too big?

153
00:10:33,240 --> 00:10:36,390
Then let's take in Ximei?

154
00:10:38,870 --> 00:10:39,480
Okay.

155
00:10:39,750 --> 00:10:40,870
Then...

156
00:10:41,960 --> 00:10:43,490
let's have a little Junnan.

157
00:10:43,600 --> 00:10:45,130
Get me a little Silly Qiang.

158
00:10:46,030 --> 00:10:47,360
Then we'll move in too,

159
00:10:47,360 --> 00:10:48,150
when the time comes.

160
00:10:48,150 --> 00:10:48,870
We'll all be together.

161
00:10:48,870 --> 00:10:49,720
We'll all be together.

162
00:10:49,720 --> 00:10:50,480
Not one less.

163
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:50,750
Right?

164
00:10:50,750 --> 00:10:51,960
-Okay.
-All together.

165
00:10:51,960 --> 00:10:53,390
What are your plans?

166
00:10:53,870 --> 00:10:54,980
I've made up my mind.

167
00:10:54,980 --> 00:10:57,270
Once I get to the city,
I'll take the college entrance exam.

168
00:10:57,270 --> 00:10:59,000
Why do you want to go to college?

169
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,320
I need to quickly change
my primary school uniform

170
00:11:00,320 --> 00:11:01,440
into a college one.

171
00:11:03,550 --> 00:11:05,610
They don't wear uniforms in college.

172
00:11:06,930 --> 00:11:07,480
Then...

173
00:11:08,440 --> 00:11:09,640
I won't take the exam.

174
00:11:09,670 --> 00:11:10,840
I'll give you an idea.

175
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:13,320
You can go to Hogwarts.

176
00:11:13,630 --> 00:11:15,430
Their uniforms are really nice.

177
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:16,480
-Yeah.
-A big cloak.

178
00:11:16,480 --> 00:11:17,210
That's good.

179
00:11:17,600 --> 00:11:18,670
That warts thing.

180
00:11:18,790 --> 00:11:19,720
-That warts thing.
-So cool.

181
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:20,450
It suits you,

182
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:21,550
especially with your hairstyle.

183
00:11:21,550 --> 00:11:22,030
Really?

184
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:23,270
Then I'll try it out.

185
00:11:23,870 --> 00:11:25,150
I've made up my mind too.

186
00:11:25,150 --> 00:11:25,610
Junnan,

187
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:26,910
I plan to

188
00:11:27,200 --> 00:11:27,960
go abroad.

189
00:11:28,040 --> 00:11:29,760
I'll tidy myself up.

190
00:11:30,670 --> 00:11:32,200
With my good looks,

191
00:11:32,200 --> 00:11:33,400
I'll become an actor.

192
00:11:34,200 --> 00:11:35,910
When I hold a concert,
you all have to come.

193
00:11:35,910 --> 00:11:36,480
When the time comes.

194
00:11:36,480 --> 00:11:37,240
Okay.

195
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:38,200
Save us

196
00:11:38,200 --> 00:11:39,750
a VIP private room.

197
00:11:40,030 --> 00:11:41,030
What P?

198
00:11:41,360 --> 00:11:42,560
Struck by lightning.

199
00:11:42,750 --> 00:11:43,320
Right.

200
00:11:44,750 --> 00:11:45,600
Wen

201
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:46,750
just doesn't know his own limits.

202
00:11:46,750 --> 00:11:47,390
You know?

203
00:11:47,550 --> 00:11:48,030
What do you mean?

204
00:11:48,030 --> 00:11:49,390
With your limited skills,

205
00:11:49,390 --> 00:11:50,480
you want to be an actor?

206
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:52,450
Wait, look at me shaking my head.

207
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:53,790
Isn't this enough?

208
00:11:53,790 --> 00:11:54,750
Isn't this enough?

209
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:56,080
Haven't you seen that foreign one?

210
00:11:56,080 --> 00:11:57,750
Aren't there 3 guys abroad?

211
00:11:57,910 --> 00:11:58,870
That Jim Carrey group,

212
00:11:58,870 --> 00:12:00,030
the ones shaking their necks,
haven't you seen them?

213
00:12:00,030 --> 00:12:01,240
Just shake.

214
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:03,120
The three of us
will shake our necks together.

215
00:12:03,120 --> 00:12:03,580
Just...

216
00:12:03,840 --> 00:12:05,150
Three foreigners,

217
00:12:05,150 --> 00:12:06,360
shaking their necks.

218
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:07,670
Who can't shake their neck?

219
00:12:07,670 --> 00:12:08,600
Anyone with a head can do it.

220
00:12:08,600 --> 00:12:09,720
Y-You can't.

221
00:12:09,720 --> 00:12:11,480
If I can, Junnan definitely can.

222
00:12:11,480 --> 00:12:12,550
Who can't do this?

223
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,480
Ximei, you be the judge.

224
00:12:14,550 --> 00:12:15,030
Come on.

225
00:12:15,030 --> 00:12:16,200
Let me see how you shake.

226
00:12:16,200 --> 00:12:16,750
Can you shake like this?

227
00:12:16,750 --> 00:12:18,000
-Why not?
-Listen to me.

228
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,150
Five, six, seven, eight.

229
00:12:26,960 --> 00:12:29,620
-Shapu Three Cute Guys!
-Shapu Three Cute Guys!

230
00:12:31,550 --> 00:12:34,210
-Shapu Three Cute Guys!
-Shapu Three Cute Guys!

231
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:37,440
Cheers!

232
00:12:48,080 --> 00:12:50,080
Chen Bingqiang,

233
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:52,390
you traitor,

234
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:54,390
you big jerk!

235
00:12:54,390 --> 00:12:55,840
And that guy named Huang,

236
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:57,750
you're not

237
00:12:57,750 --> 00:12:58,510
a good

238
00:12:59,120 --> 00:12:59,750
person

239
00:13:00,320 --> 00:13:01,150
either!

240
00:13:00,430 --> 00:13:03,620
♪ Lost in the crowds, we carry on ♪

241
00:13:02,790 --> 00:13:03,480
Brother,

242
00:13:03,720 --> 00:13:07,140
♪ Someone will stay
with you through day and night ♪

243
00:13:04,030 --> 00:13:05,790
why do I feel like scolding them like this

244
00:13:05,790 --> 00:13:06,920
doesn't relieve...

245
00:13:07,000 --> 00:13:09,200
my anger at all?

246
00:13:08,090 --> 00:13:11,410
♪ The art of loving and being loved ♪

247
00:13:11,840 --> 00:13:13,240
Chen Bingqiang!

248
00:13:12,040 --> 00:13:15,640
♪ I'll give my all
to get it right for you ♪

249
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:14,910
I f...

250
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:20,140
♪ Who would risk it all for you? ♪

251
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:17,600
Jiahao,

252
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,390
there are still kids in the village.

253
00:13:19,390 --> 00:13:20,660
It's enough that you made your point.

254
00:13:20,530 --> 00:13:23,720
♪ Locking all the sorrow deep inside ♪

255
00:13:21,490 --> 00:13:23,150
Let's not scold them anymore.

256
00:13:23,350 --> 00:13:24,680
Scolding them won't solve the problem.

257
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:27,870
♪ Like a clown who can become ♪

258
00:13:25,150 --> 00:13:26,000
Since things have come to this,

259
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:27,960
let's just look forward.

260
00:13:28,630 --> 00:13:32,500
♪ The superhero who makes you smile ♪

261
00:13:28,960 --> 00:13:30,160
Let them tear it down.

262
00:13:30,320 --> 00:13:31,630
As long as we are here
and have our skills,

263
00:13:31,630 --> 00:13:32,790
can't we still make a living?

264
00:13:32,790 --> 00:13:33,320
-Yes!
-Exactly!

265
00:13:33,320 --> 00:13:34,200
Let's go to the city.

266
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:36,390
♪ Oh, time ♪

267
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:35,240
Go to the city with me.

268
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:35,720
Yes!

269
00:13:35,790 --> 00:13:37,670
We'll continue to open
Zhen's Fish Ball in the city.

270
00:13:36,410 --> 00:13:40,210
♪ People who live like clowns ♪

271
00:13:37,720 --> 00:13:38,150
Okay!

272
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:39,670
One store will become two.

273
00:13:39,670 --> 00:13:40,750
-Okay!
-Two will become four.

274
00:13:40,510 --> 00:13:43,390
♪ Have long forgotten the dust
on their sleeves ♪

275
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,320
Four will become eight,
and then many more.

276
00:13:42,320 --> 00:13:43,670
We'll go public and start a franchise!

277
00:13:43,550 --> 00:13:48,890
♪ With honest hearts,
we make this world more tender ♪

278
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:46,600
Then we'll acquire
that Huang guy's company

279
00:13:46,750 --> 00:13:48,240
and make them all work for us!

280
00:13:48,240 --> 00:13:48,550
Okay!

281
00:13:48,550 --> 00:13:50,150
I'll make that Chen guy apologize to me!

282
00:13:48,910 --> 00:13:52,580
♪ Oh, time ♪

283
00:13:50,390 --> 00:13:51,050
Apologize!

284
00:13:51,480 --> 00:13:53,240
I'll make him clean my toilet every day!

285
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:56,770
♪ We who were once loved by clowns ♪

286
00:13:53,240 --> 00:13:53,790
Okay!

287
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:54,840
And wash my socks every day!

288
00:13:54,840 --> 00:13:55,640
-Okay!
-Okay!

289
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:56,750
Together with that Huang guy!

290
00:13:56,750 --> 00:13:57,440
Together!

291
00:13:57,280 --> 00:13:59,580
♪ Can become superheroes too ♪

292
00:13:58,030 --> 00:13:58,670
Cheers!

293
00:13:59,620 --> 00:14:05,040
♪ Saving every inch of sorrow ♪

294
00:14:00,480 --> 00:14:01,080
Cheers.

295
00:14:05,120 --> 00:14:05,790
Sister,

296
00:14:05,550 --> 00:14:09,410
♪ Then the world is whole again ♪

297
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:09,260
I will definitely make a lot of money,

298
00:14:09,440 --> 00:14:11,170
and then buy a house in the city.

299
00:14:11,510 --> 00:14:12,910
We'll buy a two-bedroom apartment.

300
00:14:12,910 --> 00:14:14,170
One room for each of us.

301
00:14:15,360 --> 00:14:16,550
What about me?

302
00:14:17,680 --> 00:14:19,280
We can sleep in bunk beds.

303
00:14:21,270 --> 00:14:23,320
You want to share a room with my sister?

304
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:24,270
No, no, no.

305
00:14:24,270 --> 00:14:25,150
I... I...

306
00:14:25,230 --> 00:14:28,430
♪ Lost in the crowds, we carry on ♪

307
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:27,030
I want to sleep on the top bunk this time.

308
00:14:27,030 --> 00:14:27,750
No problem.

309
00:14:27,750 --> 00:14:29,320
-Yeah.
-Want the top bunk.

310
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:31,940
♪ Someone will stay
with you through day and night ♪

311
00:14:32,780 --> 00:14:36,100
♪ The art of loving and being loved ♪

312
00:14:34,030 --> 00:14:34,840
Brother.

313
00:14:36,030 --> 00:14:38,670
Seeing the welfare center like this,

314
00:14:36,730 --> 00:14:40,330
♪ I'll give my all
to get it right for you ♪

315
00:14:39,390 --> 00:14:41,360
I feel a bit sad.

316
00:14:41,580 --> 00:14:44,820
♪ Who would risk it all for you? ♪

317
00:14:45,220 --> 00:14:48,400
♪ Locking all the sorrow deep inside ♪

318
00:14:48,830 --> 00:14:52,560
♪ Like a clown who can become ♪

319
00:14:49,360 --> 00:14:49,960
Sister,

320
00:14:51,270 --> 00:14:53,000
you and Zhou Ke go to the city

321
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,240
and arrange things there.

322
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:57,190
♪ The superhero who makes you smile ♪

323
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,080
Let me...

324
00:14:58,150 --> 00:15:01,070
♪ Oh, time ♪

325
00:14:59,670 --> 00:15:01,100
tear down the welfare center myself.

326
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:04,900
♪ People who live like clowns ♪

327
00:15:03,510 --> 00:15:05,360
Can you do it alone?

328
00:15:05,190 --> 00:15:08,070
♪ Have long forgotten the dust
on their sleeves ♪

329
00:15:07,630 --> 00:15:08,510
No problem.

330
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:13,570
♪ With honest hearts,
we make this world more tender ♪

331
00:15:08,750 --> 00:15:09,410
No problem.

332
00:15:10,320 --> 00:15:11,780
We'll go to the city first.

333
00:15:12,480 --> 00:15:13,600
We're counting on you here.

334
00:15:13,600 --> 00:15:17,260
♪ Oh, time ♪

335
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,180
See you in the city.

336
00:15:16,000 --> 00:15:16,600
Cheers!

337
00:15:16,620 --> 00:15:17,220
Cheers.

338
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:21,460
♪ We who were once loved by clowns ♪

339
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:18,980
To the welfare center.

340
00:15:21,970 --> 00:15:24,270
♪ Can become superheroes too ♪

341
00:15:24,300 --> 00:15:29,730
♪ Saving every inch of sorrow ♪

342
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:26,600
Cheers.

343
00:15:27,200 --> 00:15:27,790
Cheers.

344
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,320
Sweetheart.

345
00:15:55,480 --> 00:15:56,540
What are you doing?

346
00:15:57,150 --> 00:15:59,390
Is everything going well in Shapu Village?

347
00:15:59,390 --> 00:16:01,150
Not bad. Everything is going well.

348
00:16:01,150 --> 00:16:02,550
When are you coming back?

349
00:16:03,870 --> 00:16:04,480
Soon.

350
00:16:04,480 --> 00:16:06,610
I'll be back as soon as I finish up here.

351
00:16:07,790 --> 00:16:09,150
Are you

352
00:16:09,150 --> 00:16:11,720
rekindling your old romance with Zhen?

353
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:14,510
How is that possible?
What are you talking about?

354
00:16:14,510 --> 00:16:16,360
How many times have I told you?

355
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,720
You are the only one in my heart.

356
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:20,730
Alright, I'm just teasing you.

357
00:16:22,170 --> 00:16:24,320
I originally wanted to tell you something,

358
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:25,720
but then I was afraid

359
00:16:26,550 --> 00:16:27,840
you weren't ready.

360
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,870
Forget it. You're coming back soon anyway.

361
00:16:30,870 --> 00:16:32,200
Let's talk face to face when you get back.

362
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,360
Don't do that. Just tell me now.

363
00:16:33,360 --> 00:16:34,150
You're keeping me in suspense.

364
00:16:34,150 --> 00:16:35,670
I won't be able to sleep tonight.

365
00:16:35,670 --> 00:16:36,240
Hello?

366
00:16:36,910 --> 00:16:37,510
Hello?

367
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,270
Jiahao.

368
00:17:12,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Have you eaten?

369
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:15,480
How about

370
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:17,079
I treat you to something?

371
00:17:22,069 --> 00:17:22,750
You know,

372
00:17:22,859 --> 00:17:25,690
our village has a unified demolition team.

373
00:17:26,240 --> 00:17:28,440
Why do you have to work so hard?

374
00:17:29,550 --> 00:17:31,400
I know you're unhappy.

375
00:17:32,310 --> 00:17:33,550
In this situation—

376
00:17:33,550 --> 00:17:34,920
Do you need something?

377
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,200
If not, leave.

378
00:17:36,230 --> 00:17:37,070
I'm working.

379
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:40,070
Just chatting.

380
00:17:40,510 --> 00:17:41,350
Where is Zhen?

381
00:17:43,350 --> 00:17:44,480
She went to the city.

382
00:17:44,680 --> 00:17:47,080
She never wants
to see you again in her life.

383
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:47,920
Me neither.

384
00:17:49,950 --> 00:17:52,920
Jiahao, you guys really misunderstood me.

385
00:17:53,550 --> 00:17:54,990
Think about it carefully.

386
00:17:54,990 --> 00:17:57,990
You caused the villagers
to lose so much money.

387
00:17:58,100 --> 00:18:00,420
I managed to invite Mr. Huang over

388
00:18:00,990 --> 00:18:03,320
to cover the villagers' losses.

389
00:18:04,400 --> 00:18:08,260
The demolition project
also compensated the villagers generously.

390
00:18:09,590 --> 00:18:10,850
I can't control it well.

391
00:18:10,850 --> 00:18:12,780
I won't be responsible if I hit you.

392
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:17,860
I'll go check on other houses.

393
00:18:20,510 --> 00:18:21,310
Wait, Jiahao!

394
00:18:21,330 --> 00:18:22,790
Jiahao, you dug something up!

395
00:18:22,790 --> 00:18:24,510
Don't! Stop, stop!

396
00:18:25,670 --> 00:18:26,580
What are you doing?

397
00:18:26,580 --> 00:18:27,780
You dug something up!

398
00:18:28,280 --> 00:18:29,200
What is it?

399
00:18:30,510 --> 00:18:31,440
It seems to be...

400
00:18:33,640 --> 00:18:34,200
This...

401
00:18:34,640 --> 00:18:35,570
Could this be...

402
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:47,790
Oh my god.

403
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:53,160
Did...

404
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:55,830
Did we dig up someone's ancestral grave?

405
00:18:56,350 --> 00:18:58,220
Based on what I know about our village,

406
00:18:58,220 --> 00:19:00,830
no household could have such good stuff.

407
00:19:06,370 --> 00:19:08,050
What Mr. Maling said is true.

408
00:19:11,350 --> 00:19:13,070
I've heard Mr. Maling
say since I was a kid

409
00:19:13,070 --> 00:19:14,310
that there was some treasure.

410
00:19:14,310 --> 00:19:16,000
T-Treasure.

411
00:19:18,790 --> 00:19:20,480
Never mind who said it!

412
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:21,920
These are treasures!

413
00:19:22,400 --> 00:19:23,350
If I sell them for money,

414
00:19:23,350 --> 00:19:24,270
I won't have to do the demolition!

415
00:19:24,270 --> 00:19:25,030
Wait a minute!

416
00:19:25,030 --> 00:19:26,160
Your thought is very dangerous,

417
00:19:26,160 --> 00:19:27,020
let me tell you.

418
00:19:27,240 --> 00:19:28,270
If they're real,

419
00:19:28,270 --> 00:19:29,350
they belong to the state.

420
00:19:29,350 --> 00:19:30,440
If you sell them, you're breaking the law.

421
00:19:30,440 --> 00:19:31,510
You'll go to jail.

422
00:19:34,070 --> 00:19:34,640
Then...

423
00:19:36,790 --> 00:19:38,110
Then I'll call the government right away.

424
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:39,030
I don't want to sell them.

425
00:19:39,030 --> 00:19:39,830
I want to hand them over.

426
00:19:39,830 --> 00:19:40,630
Wait a minute!

427
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:43,100
Your idea is even more dangerous.

428
00:19:43,290 --> 00:19:44,420
What if they're fake

429
00:19:44,880 --> 00:19:45,880
and you call the government people here?

430
00:19:45,880 --> 00:19:47,350
They travel all this way.

431
00:19:47,350 --> 00:19:49,000
So many people come and take a look,

432
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:50,000
and they're fake.

433
00:19:50,200 --> 00:19:51,640
You'd be fabricating,

434
00:19:51,880 --> 00:19:53,440
guilty of intentionally
spreading false information.

435
00:19:53,440 --> 00:19:54,770
You'll still go to jail.

436
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,400
Then what should I do?

437
00:19:56,590 --> 00:19:57,640
I'm not...

438
00:19:58,440 --> 00:19:59,400
Alright, then I'll bury them back.

439
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:00,460
Alright, alright.

440
00:20:00,920 --> 00:20:02,090
I'll be lenient

441
00:20:02,120 --> 00:20:03,180
and save your life.

442
00:20:03,530 --> 00:20:05,530
I'll go find some appraisal experts

443
00:20:05,560 --> 00:20:06,490
to verify them first.

444
00:20:06,490 --> 00:20:07,420
If they're real,

445
00:20:07,640 --> 00:20:08,750
we'll hand them over to the government.

446
00:20:08,750 --> 00:20:09,830
No, no, no way.

447
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:12,710
What if you find out they're real

448
00:20:12,740 --> 00:20:13,910
and take them away?

449
00:20:13,930 --> 00:20:15,460
What if you don't come back?

450
00:20:16,030 --> 00:20:17,000
Chen Jiahao.

451
00:20:17,510 --> 00:20:18,790
We've been brothers for so many years,

452
00:20:18,790 --> 00:20:20,310
and you don't trust my character?

453
00:20:20,310 --> 00:20:21,400
I don't trust you.

454
00:20:24,230 --> 00:20:25,300
I can see it now.

455
00:20:25,470 --> 00:20:26,920
I can see it now.

456
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:30,620
You just want to keep it
for yourself, right?

457
00:20:30,790 --> 00:20:32,110
Keep it for myself?

458
00:20:32,110 --> 00:20:33,240
If I weren't here today,

459
00:20:33,240 --> 00:20:34,480
you would have already kept it.

460
00:20:34,480 --> 00:20:35,590
Don't make false accusations!

461
00:20:35,590 --> 00:20:37,790
Then why won't you let me appraise them?

462
00:20:38,640 --> 00:20:39,350
Why?

463
00:20:39,590 --> 00:20:40,240
Why?

464
00:20:40,650 --> 00:20:42,650
Then you take one first!

465
00:20:45,000 --> 00:20:45,480
Such a hassle.

466
00:20:45,480 --> 00:20:46,280
Wait a minute!

467
00:20:46,350 --> 00:20:47,080
Put it there!

468
00:20:48,020 --> 00:20:48,640
What's wrong now?

469
00:20:48,640 --> 00:20:49,560
I have to record you.

470
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:52,460
If you dare to run,
I'll call the police to arrest you.

471
00:20:52,460 --> 00:20:53,110
Wait.

472
00:20:53,140 --> 00:20:54,800
Wait, the camera didn't flip.

473
00:20:56,410 --> 00:20:57,040
Speak.

474
00:20:57,640 --> 00:20:59,510
I, Chen Bingqiang,

475
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:01,590
am now taking a bowl for appraisal.

476
00:21:01,590 --> 00:21:03,070
If this is real,

477
00:21:03,270 --> 00:21:05,000
I absolutely won't keep it for myself.

478
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,030
I'll hand it directly to the government.

479
00:21:07,030 --> 00:21:07,790
Is that okay?

480
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:12,350
Okay.

481
00:21:12,720 --> 00:21:13,450
I'm leaving.

482
00:21:14,230 --> 00:21:15,830
Don't dig before I come back.

483
00:21:16,880 --> 00:21:19,550
P-Protect it well.

484
00:21:19,830 --> 00:21:21,310
Put it in your pocket!

485
00:21:29,350 --> 00:21:30,110
Mr. Huang.

486
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:31,880
Fake.

487
00:21:37,610 --> 00:21:40,810
This is obviously a 2005 replica.

488
00:21:41,790 --> 00:21:43,590
Who told you to verify this?

489
00:21:44,410 --> 00:21:45,330
Verify this.

490
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:47,960
My eyes are blurry.

491
00:21:47,990 --> 00:21:49,750
I thought it was an ashtray.

492
00:21:51,130 --> 00:21:52,400
Where is he from?

493
00:21:52,430 --> 00:21:53,640
Who invited him?

494
00:21:53,660 --> 00:21:54,420
I did.

495
00:21:55,830 --> 00:21:57,030
Mr. Gao is our local master

496
00:21:57,030 --> 00:21:58,550
of cultural relic appraisal.

497
00:21:58,550 --> 00:21:59,350
Mr. Gao.

498
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:01,720
He's really something.
He looks professional.

499
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:02,990
Look at this thing.

500
00:22:08,010 --> 00:22:09,010
How is it, Mr. Gao?

501
00:22:10,000 --> 00:22:10,640
This...

502
00:22:11,200 --> 00:22:12,120
is authentic.

503
00:22:12,360 --> 00:22:15,820
An artifact from the early Jiajing period
of the Ming Dynasty.

504
00:22:16,590 --> 00:22:18,310
It's worth at least...

505
00:22:19,710 --> 00:22:20,950
7 figures.

506
00:22:26,640 --> 00:22:28,160
Long live Mr. Gao.

507
00:22:28,480 --> 00:22:30,540
You've worked really hard this time.

508
00:22:30,790 --> 00:22:31,350
Mr. Gao.

509
00:22:33,610 --> 00:22:35,850
The 2015-edition RMB banknotes.

510
00:22:36,270 --> 00:22:37,030
Quick, touch me.

511
00:22:37,030 --> 00:22:38,200
Touch me and see what year I am.

512
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:39,400
Come here, come here.

513
00:22:41,000 --> 00:22:41,960
Oh my god.

514
00:22:43,030 --> 00:22:44,960
Mr. Maling told us when we were kids

515
00:22:45,690 --> 00:22:49,070
that when Qi Jiguang fought
the Japanese pirates in the Ming Dynasty,

516
00:22:49,070 --> 00:22:51,880
a group of defeated pirates

517
00:22:52,550 --> 00:22:55,550
buried a large amount of treasure
near Shapu Village.

518
00:22:56,440 --> 00:22:57,790
It's actually true.

519
00:23:00,270 --> 00:23:02,590
But how do we sell this authentic thing?

520
00:23:02,590 --> 00:23:04,750
We'll get caught as soon as we sell it.

521
00:23:06,590 --> 00:23:08,590
We don't have the channels for this.

522
00:23:10,110 --> 00:23:11,110
What should we do?

523
00:23:11,240 --> 00:23:12,510
Don't worry.

524
00:23:13,480 --> 00:23:15,340
There are many ways to solve this.

525
00:23:15,680 --> 00:23:16,480
Auctions,

526
00:23:16,840 --> 00:23:17,860
offline transactions,

527
00:23:17,860 --> 00:23:19,190
or through a middleman.

528
00:23:20,240 --> 00:23:22,240
As long as this thing gets out,

529
00:23:22,530 --> 00:23:24,260
you can use any method you want.

530
00:23:26,750 --> 00:23:27,790
The day after tomorrow.

531
00:23:27,790 --> 00:23:29,190
I plan to buy a speedboat.

532
00:23:30,510 --> 00:23:32,160
Customs anti-smuggling?

533
00:23:32,180 --> 00:23:32,970
Let me tell you,

534
00:23:32,970 --> 00:23:35,210
even the Jiaolong squad can't stop me.

535
00:23:36,510 --> 00:23:37,350
Rest assured.

536
00:23:37,880 --> 00:23:40,210
You just need to have an overseas account,

537
00:23:40,650 --> 00:23:41,570
and that's it.

538
00:23:48,260 --> 00:23:50,590
After years of enduring hardship
and biding my time,

539
00:23:50,590 --> 00:23:53,000
my luck has finally turned.

540
00:23:53,920 --> 00:23:55,070
Just a reminder.

541
00:23:55,790 --> 00:23:56,790
It's our luck.

542
00:23:59,750 --> 00:24:00,680
What do you mean?

543
00:24:03,270 --> 00:24:06,160
I discovered these treasures,

544
00:24:06,720 --> 00:24:08,110
and I dug them out,

545
00:24:09,050 --> 00:24:11,050
risking my life to bring them to you.

546
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:12,800
Getting a share of the pie

547
00:24:13,070 --> 00:24:14,670
isn't too much to ask, right?

548
00:24:17,480 --> 00:24:18,430
How about half a cup?

549
00:24:18,430 --> 00:24:19,120
Deal.

550
00:24:24,330 --> 00:24:25,920
I should have said a sip.

551
00:24:33,590 --> 00:24:35,050
I had someone appraise it.

552
00:24:35,240 --> 00:24:35,880
It's fake.

553
00:24:36,480 --> 00:24:37,410
Really?

554
00:24:37,830 --> 00:24:38,480
Really.

555
00:24:38,750 --> 00:24:39,480
Really real?

556
00:24:39,720 --> 00:24:40,920
It's fake.

557
00:24:41,220 --> 00:24:42,390
Is it real or fake?

558
00:24:42,410 --> 00:24:43,140
Fake.

559
00:24:43,410 --> 00:24:45,010
Fake. Couldn't be more fake.

560
00:24:47,270 --> 00:24:47,730
This...

561
00:24:48,130 --> 00:24:49,790
Who did you ask to appraise it?

562
00:24:50,120 --> 00:24:52,250
Our local artifact appraisal master.

563
00:24:53,000 --> 00:24:53,930
What's his name?

564
00:24:54,510 --> 00:24:55,160
Mr. Gao.

565
00:24:55,880 --> 00:24:56,590
Mr. Gao?

566
00:25:01,480 --> 00:25:03,080
I'll go find someone myself.

567
00:25:09,750 --> 00:25:10,640
This is real.

568
00:25:16,360 --> 00:25:17,360
Chen Bingqiang.

569
00:25:18,750 --> 00:25:20,610
You were trying to trick me again.

570
00:25:21,960 --> 00:25:23,620
My sister told me everything.

571
00:25:24,030 --> 00:25:25,440
I'm not stupid at all.

572
00:25:25,840 --> 00:25:27,710
As long as I use my brain a little,

573
